13or|n|One of the bones, usually bearing teeth, which form the framework of the mouth. ; Hence, also, the bone itself with the teeth and covering. ; In the plural, the mouth. ; Fig.: Anything resembling the jaw of an animal in form or action; esp., pl., the mouth or way of entrance; as, the jaws of a pass; the jaws of darkness; the jaws of death. ; A notch or opening. ; A notched or forked part, adapted for holding an object in place; as, the jaw of a railway-car pedestal. See Axle guard. ; One of a pair of opposing parts which are movable towards or from each other, for grasping or crushing anything between them, as, the jaws of a vise, or the jaws of a stone-crushing machine. ; The inner end of a boom or gaff, hollowed in a half circle so as to move freely on a mast. ; Impudent or abusive talk.	a:tze,140,1;t5s,118,2;267e,58,5;16y3,43,5;8qq,35,2;1urr,29,5;ohj,12,2;1era,6,4~1urr,29,5;16y3,43,5;267e,58,5;1era,6,4;ohj,12,2;8qq,35,2;t5s,118,2;tze,140,1	v:t5s,108,1~t5s,108,1	V:md2,51,1;md0,48,1~md2,51,1;md0,48,1	n:tze,140,1;267e,45,2~267e,45,2;tze,140,1	N:1mr9,94,2;8in,77,3;1b56,52,2;1e3t,38,2;33s,27,1;1v0x,4,1~8in,77,3;1e3t,38,2;1mr9,94,2;1b56,52,2;1v0x,4,1;33s,27,1
